flowchart TB
    accTitle: Detectra user flow adapted from the original Figma design
    accDescr: Main manual journey through upload or camera Scan Now, analysis, saved results, optional review, and confirmed feedback. This adaptation reflects the implemented multiclass application and local image storage. Automatic camera saving is a separate optional background workflow.
    I{"Input?"}
    I -->|Image| U["Select a valid image<br/>Click Analyze Image"]
    I -->|Camera| C["Open Camera Scan<br/>Connect camera · Click Scan Now"]
    U --> A["Analyze and save results<br/>Show detections and confidence,<br/>or no detections"]
    C --> A
    A --> Q{"Review?"}
    Q -->|Yes| F["Select reviewer · Review result<br/>Choose Correct or Incorrect"]
    F --> S{"Saved?"}
    S -->|Yes| P["Show saved feedback<br/>Retained after reload"]
    S -->|No| E["Show feedback error<br/>Retry submission"]
    E --> F
    P --> N["Analyze or scan again,<br/>or return home"]
    Q -->|Not now| N
    N --> I

